    "title": "pandas.Index.to_list — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.to_list#\n\n- Index.to_list()[source]#\n- Return a list of the values. These are each a scalar type, which is a Python scalar (for str, int, float) or a pandas scalar (for Timestamp/Timedelta/Interval/Period) \n  - Returns:\n    - list\n    - List containing the values as Python or pandas scalers.\n See also \n  - `numpy.ndarray.tolist`\n  - Return the array as an a.ndim-levels deep nested list of Python scalars.\n Examples For Series >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3]) >>> s.to_list() [1, 2, 3] For Index: >>> idx = pd.Index([1, 2, 3]) >>> idx Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64') >>> idx.to_list() [1, 2, 3]",
